  "content": "<p>Check your understanding of CNC routing. Your answers aren't recorded.</p><multiple-choice question=\"In 2.5D milling, what can't a straight end mill cut, whatever the toolpath?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"An inside corner sharper than the bit's radius\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"A pocket deeper than half the stock\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"A curved outline\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"Lettering\">\n</multiple-choice><multiple-choice question=\"What are tabs for in a profile cut?\" single-option=\"\" randomize=\"\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"They hold the part to the stock so it can't shift or fly loose as the cut finishes\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"They mark where the cut starts\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"They cool the bit\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"They stop tear-out on the top face\">\n</multiple-choice><true-false-question question=\"Feeds and speeds only change how long a job takes, not the quality or safety of the cut.\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"False\" data-correct=\"true\">\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" value=\"True\">\n</true-false-question><self-check title=\"Think it through\">\n  <p slot=\"question\">Before you start a CNC job, what do you check about zero?</p>\n  <p>That X and Y zero are where the CAM setup expects them (a corner or the centre of the stock), and that Z zero is set to the surface the CAM used (the top of the stock or the spoilboard). A mismatch cuts air, or cuts into the spoilboard.</p>\n</self-check>"
}